.TH "errors" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
errors \- the error values of the library and the limits of a build
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SS "Classes"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBcbor::error_category\fP"
.br
.RI "The \fRstd::error_category\fP of \fBcbor::error\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBstd::is_error_code_enum< cbor::error >\fP"
.br
.RI "Marks \fBcbor::error\fP as an error code enum\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "struct \fBcbor::limits\fP"
.br
.RI "Gives the limits of the build\&. "
.in -1c
.SS "Enumerations"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "enum class \fBcbor::error\fP { \fBerror::too_little_data\fP = 1, \fBerror::syntax_error\fP, \fBerror::indefinite_length\fP, \fBerror::nesting_depth_exceeded\fP, \fBerror::inadmissible_type_for_tag_content\fP, \fBerror::sharedref_index_not_marked\fP, \fBerror::sharedref_not_complete\fP, \fBerror::sharedref_not_defined\fP, \fBerror::reserved_simple_value\fP, \fBerror::unsupported_value\fP, \fBerror::not_indexable\fP, \fBerror::index_out_of_bounds\fP, \fBerror::key_not_found\fP, \fBerror::invalid_path\fP, \fBerror::incorrect_type\fP, \fBerror::number_out_of_range\fP, \fBerror::cyclic_data_structure\fP, \fBerror::unpopulated_table_index\fP, \fBerror::nodelist_too_long\fP, \fBerror::duplicate_key\fP, \fBerror::no_buffer_space\fP, \fBerror::value_too_large\fP, \fBerror::not_enough_memory\fP, \fBerror::io_error\fP, \fBerror::string_length_exceeded\fP, \fBerror::container_elements_exceeded\fP, \fBerror::not_singular_query\fP, \fBerror::amplification_limit_breach\fP }"
.br
.RI "Names the fault that a call returns in its \fRstd::expected<T, \fBcbor::error\fP>\fP\&. "
.in -1c
.SS "Functions"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "std::error_category const & \fBcbor::category\fP () noexcept"
.br
.RI "Gives the one \fBcbor::error_category\fP of \fBcbor::error\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "std::error_code \fBcbor::make_error_code\fP (\fBerror\fP const e) noexcept"
.br
.RI "Makes a \fRstd::error_code\fP with the value of \fRe\fP and the \fBcbor::category()\fP of \fBcbor::error\fP\&. "
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
A call that reads CBOR gives a \fRstd::expected\fP with a \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP when it fails\&. Bad input never throws\&. The \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP names the fault\&. Include \fR<\fBcbor/cbor\&.hpp\fP>\fP\&.

.PP
A \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP converts to a \fRstd::error_code\fP of the category \fR\fBcbor::category()\fP\fP\&. The message of that \fRstd::error_code\fP is the text of the fault\&.

.PP
A limit of the build stops input that holds a string or a container that is too large\&. A macro sets each limit\&. \fR\fBcbor::limits\fP\fP gives its value\&.
.SH "THE ERROR VALUES"
.PP
Each value is one enumerator of \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRtoo_little_data\fP: the bytes end before the item ends\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsyntax_error\fP: a head is not well-formed, or a simple value is reserved in the two-byte form\&. A call that reads exactly one item finds bytes after it: \fR\fBcbor::diagnostic_notation\fP\fP and the content of a tag 24\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRindefinite_length\fP: a head uses indefinite length, and the call does not read it\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnesting_depth_exceeded\fP: a reader that recurses reaches the end of the stack of its thread (\fR\fBcbor::limits\fP\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRinadmissible_type_for_tag_content\fP: a tag has content that its definition does not allow\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsharedref_index_not_marked\fP: a tag 29 names no tag 28 before it\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsharedref_not_complete\fP: \fR\fBcbor::structs\fP\fP decode meets a tag 29 that names a tag 28 in a skipped member\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsharedref_not_defined\fP: \fR\fBcbor::decode\fP\fP meets a tag 29 that names a tag 28 whose content is only tags 28 and this tag 29\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRreserved_simple_value\fP: an encode meets a simple value from 24 to 31\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRunsupported_value\fP: the encoder meets a typed array with a reserved tag, or a tag outside RFC 8746; \fR\fBcbor::encode()\fP\fP writes a tag 29 only with \fR\fBcbor::cycles\fP\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnot_indexable\fP: a key or an index meets an item that is not a map or an array\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRindex_out_of_bounds\fP: the index is outside the array\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRkey_not_found\fP: the key is not in the map\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRinvalid_path\fP: the text of a path is not valid\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRincorrect_type\fP: a typed read finds another kind of item than the type \fRT\fP takes\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnumber_out_of_range\fP: the number does not fit \fRT\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRcyclic_data_structure\fP: the library does not return it\&. A writer of the program can return it for a cycle\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRunpopulated_table_index\fP: a reference in a \fRcbor::schema<T>\fP message names an entry that its table does not have\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnodelist_too_long\fP: one step of a path selects more nodes than the item has bytes\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRduplicate_key\fP: a deterministic check finds a key twice in one map\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRno_buffer_space\fP: the writer of an encode gives this error\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRvalue_too_large\fP: the writer of an encode gives this error\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnot_enough_memory\fP: the writer of an encode gives this error\&. A refused allocation in \fR\fBcbor::structs\fP\fP or \fRcbor::schema\fP decode gives it too\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRio_error\fP: the writer of an encode gives this error\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstring_length_exceeded\fP: a string is longer than \fR\fBcbor::limits::string_length\fP\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRcontainer_elements_exceeded\fP: a container has more items than \fR\fBcbor::limits::container_elements\fP\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnot_singular_query\fP: \fRcbor::path::compile<T>\fP gets a path that is not singular, and \fRT\fP is not \fRnodelist\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRamplification_limit_breach\fP: \fR\fBcbor::encode()\fP\fP with \fR\fBcbor::cycles\fP\fP would write more than \fR\fBcbor::limits::maximum_amplification\fP\fP times the size of the tree, past \fR\fBcbor::limits::amplification_activation_threshold\fP\fP\&.
.PP
.SH "THE CONVERSION TO std::error_code"
.PP
\fRstd::is_error_code_enum\fP is true for \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP\&. So a \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP converts to a \fRstd::error_code\fP with no cast\&. \fR\fBcbor::make_error_code()\fP\fP makes the same value\&. A program seldom calls it by name\&.

.PP
A \fRstd::error_code\fP compares equal to a \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP with \fR==\fP\&.

.PP
The category is \fR\fBcbor::category()\fP\fP\&. Its name is \fRcbor\fP\&. Each call gives the same object\&. Its \fRmessage()\fP gives the text of an error\&. A value that is no \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP gives \fRunknown cbor error\fP\&.

.PP
Four values of \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP compare equal to a \fRstd::errc\fP:\fRno_buffer_space\fP, \fRvalue_too_large\fP, \fRnot_enough_memory\fP and \fRio_error\fP\&. Each one compares equal to the \fRstd::errc\fP of the same name\&. No other error compares equal to a \fRstd::errc\fP\&.

.PP
A \fR\fBcbor::error\fP\fP and a \fRstd::errc\fP do not compare directly\&. The direct comparison does not compile\&. Put the \fRstd::error_code\fP on the left\&.
.SH "WRONG USE"
.PP
A wrong use of the library does not compile where the compiler can see it\&. For example, a temporary \fRstd::string\fP as the bytes of a view does not compile\&.

.PP
Where the compiler cannot see a wrong use, the library throws \fRstd::logic_error\fP\&. For example:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
an empty owner, or a null \fRstd::shared_ptr<std::string const>\fP;
.IP "\(bu" 2
a \fR\fBcbor::lazy\fP{}\fP that holds no item\&.
.PP

.PP
\fRstd::logic_error\fP is a fault of the program, not of the input\&.
.SH "THE LIMITS OF A BUILD"
.PP
Each limit is a \fRstatic constexpr\fP member of \fR\fBcbor::limits\fP\fP\&. No call reads a limit at run time\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRCBOR_STRING_LENGTH_DEFAULT\fP sets \fR\fBcbor::limits::string_length\fP\fP\&. It counts the bytes of one text or byte string\&. Its error is \fRstring_length_exceeded\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRCBOR_CONTAINER_ELEMENTS_DEFAULT\fP sets \fR\fBcbor::limits::container_elements\fP\fP\&. It counts the elements of one array, or the pairs of one map\&. Its error is \fRcontainer_elements_exceeded\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRCBOR_AMPLIFICATION_ACTIVATION_THRESHOLD_DEFAULT\fP sets \fR\fBcbor::limits::amplification_activation_threshold\fP\fP\&. Its default is 8388608 bytes (8 MiB)\&. Its error is \fRamplification_limit_breach\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRCBOR_MAXIMUM_AMPLIFICATION_DEFAULT\fP sets \fR\fBcbor::limits::maximum_amplification\fP\fP\&. Its default is 100\&. Its error is \fRamplification_limit_breach\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
A macro that the build does not set takes its default\&. The default of the first two limits is \fRSIZE_MAX\fP\&. A limit at \fRSIZE_MAX\fP is not set, and its check is not in the program\&. Every translation unit of one program uses the same values\&. A value that does not fit \fRstd::size_t\fP does not compile\&.

.PP
\fR\fBcbor::encode()\fP\fP with \fR\fBcbor::cycles\fP\fP gives \fRamplification_limit_breach\fP, and writes nothing, when the output would be larger than \fR\fBcbor::limits::amplification_activation_threshold\fP\fP and than \fR\fBcbor::limits::maximum_amplification\fP\fP times the tree\&.

.PP
A limit counts what a call reads or decodes\&. An item that a call only skips does not count\&. The error comes at the read that meets the value\&. A count in the input reserves no memory\&. The library does not bound the size of the input\&. The program bounds it before it calls the library\&.

.PP
Nesting has no fixed limit\&. A reader that recurses stops where the stack of its thread ends\&. A call that comes within 16 KiB of the end of the stack gives \fRnesting_depth_exceeded\fP\&. On Windows, and with a sanitizer, the distance is 32 KiB\&.

.PP
Each thread reads the bounds of its own stack once, at its first check\&. On Linux (glibc and musl), macOS and Windows, the bounds come from the system\&. On WebAssembly without threads, and on picolibc, they come from the linker\&. Another target does not compile\&.

.PP
A frame outside these bounds, such as the stack of a fiber or of a signal handler, is not checked\&. The first check of a thread does not run in a signal handler\&. On Linux, a change of \fRRLIMIT_STACK\fP after the first check is outside the bound\&. So is a mapping that a program places with \fRMAP_FIXED\fP below the stack of the main thread\&. On picolibc, a stack smaller than the reserve refuses every nested item\&.

.PP
\fR\fBcbor::item_size()\fP\fP, \fR\fBcbor::sequence_reader\fP\fP and a path of child segments do not recurse, so they read any depth\&. A deep value of a user type that \fR\fBcbor::structs\fP\fP or \fRcbor::schema\fP reads is destroyed and copied by its own recursion\&. A thread with a smaller stack than the one that decoded the value can overflow there\&.

.PP
 
.SH "EXAMPLES"
 
.PP
.nf
    // bytes: a std::string with {"a": 1}
    auto const doc = cbor::lazy::adopt(std::move(bytes));
    auto const e = doc\->at("b")\&.error();                     // key_not_found
    std::error_code const code{e};
    std::string const text = code\&.message();                 // "key not found"
.fi
.PP
 
